        "rationale": "R1-R8/R11: port claude#617's bounded forward-compatibility into the authority. Adds _tolerant_mapping returning (known, extras), _extras_serialized_size, the 64 KiB document-total and 4x archived-fence capacity constants, and threads an `extras` field through Lease, SettlementRecord, ResourceFence, SessionAdmission, OwnerAdmissionClose, and Registry with merge-last to_dict. Exactly six _closed_mapping call sites convert; four stay strict (worktree resource_ref, settlement close, legacy settlement close, settlement recovery intent) because they are digest-covered commitment records or hash-bound resource references where every byte is semantics. FencingToken is a fifth strict boundary enforced by an inline exact-shape check at each embedding site rather than inside from_dict. U3 replaces the settlement-close CAS rebuild with replace(head, close_receipt=close) \u2014 the rebuild dropped a newer writer's per-fence extras at exactly the commit that archives the fence \u2014 and bounds the archived-fence sidecar read, which previously took a single 65536-byte read and silently truncated. U4 adds _extras_inventory, _document_extras_bytes, _strip_extras, doctor, repair, and _backup_registry. Codex-adapt rather than direct-port: the codex authority is 4249 lines against claude's 4731 and diverges outside this port's scope; a byte-copy would import ~21-30 lines of claude#616 `isolation` semantics that R9 forbids.",
